      children: "Performance architecture is similarly structural. The most impactful performance decisions - caching strategy, database indexing approach, synchronous vs. asynchronous processing, data locality - are made at the architecture level, not the code level. A system with a well-designed caching tier can handle orders of magnitude more traffic than the same system without one, regardless of how optimized the application code is. This is why premature micro-optimization of code is often wasteful: architectural performance improvements have leverage that code-level improvements do not."
    }), "\n", _jsx(_components.h2, {
