      }), " If your team structure does not match your desired architecture, you will continuously fight the organizational grain. A single team owning a dozen microservices will be pulled toward treating them as a distributed monolith - because every change requires coordinating with yourself. Conversely, multiple teams forced to share a monolith will produce a tightly coupled, unmaintainable mess - because each team optimizes locally. Architectural planning must include organizational planning."]
    }), "\n", _jsxs(_components.p, {
