            children: "Start with the quality attribute requirements, not the pattern."
          }), " Before choosing between microservices and a monolith, between event-driven and request-response, between SQL and NoSQL, understand what the system actually needs to achieve. What are the availability requirements? What is the acceptable latency at the 99th percentile? What is the expected growth trajectory? What are the security and compliance constraints? These requirements are the criteria against which architectural choices should be evaluated. Choosing a pattern because it is fashionable or because a well-known company uses it is not engineering - it is cargo-culting."]
