            children: "Use the strangler fig pattern for evolutionary migration."
          }), " When modernizing an existing system, the approach described by Martin Fowler as the Strangler Fig pattern - incrementally migrating functionality from the old system to the new one, routing traffic gradually, until the old system can be decommissioned - is almost always superior to a \"big bang\" rewrite. Rewrites are high-risk: they take longer than estimated, they miss undocumented behavior in the original system, and they require a long period of parallel operation. Incremental migration maintains a working system throughout and delivers value continuously."]
