            children: "Design for observability from the start."
          }), " A system you cannot observe is a system you cannot reliably operate or debug. Observability has three pillars - logs, metrics, and traces - and all three are architectural concerns. Structured logging (JSON output with consistent field names) must be a standard from day one. Metrics instrumentation (Prometheus, StatsD, or CloudWatch) must be part of every service's interface contract. Distributed tracing (OpenTelemetry) must propagate trace context across service boundaries. These are not features you add later; retrofitting them into a system without them is expensive and often incomplete."]
