      }), " A city is not designed all at once; it evolves over time, with earlier decisions constraining later ones. Road widths, zoning rules, and utility placements made in 1950 still determine what is possible in 2025. Software architecture has the same property. The decisions made in the first six months of a system's life - the database choice, the module structure, the API contract format - constrain every decision made afterward. City planning teaches us to think about long-term consequences of early decisions and to design infrastructure (roads, utilities) that supports future growth rather than optimizing only for current needs."]
